Description: A polygenic score built in one population usually predicts less
    accurately in another.  This package computes the best accuracy any such
    score can reach in a population, which is the share of the trait's variance
    that is genetic, and the ratio of those ceilings between two populations,
    which is their intrinsic transferability.  The ceiling is set by three
    quantities: the additive genetic variance fixed by the allele-frequency
    spectrum, the average self-kinship summarising within-population structure,
    and the non-genetic variance.  Functions are provided to evaluate the closed
    form, to simulate traits on real or simulated genotypes and measure
    transferability from them, and to draw the resulting figures.  Method
    described in Zhang, Storey and Akey (2026).
